      "Policy filtering at international gateway layer — all 4 ISP gateways (TIC x2, Irancell, Asiatech) return \"connection refused\" or TCP timeout while BGP routes remain intact — signature of centralized gateway filtering per Bock et al. FOCI'20",
      "Protocol whitelist enforcement at national gateway — only 43/1068 Iranian IP ranges (4.0%) reachable from external vantage; UDP/ICMP/SSH/VPN dropped, only DNS/HTTP/HTTPS pass — matches Iran's protocol whitelister reverse-engineered by Bock et al.",
      "Electro DNS consistently timing out — targeted pressure on anti-censorship DNS infrastructure persists",
      "Asiatech dual failure persists (gateway DROP + web portal timeout) — ISP-specific isolation on AS49666 sustained, likely CRA directive or chronic infrastructure degradation",
      "Domestic QoS discrimination — foreign platforms (Google, GitHub, Cloudflare, YouTube) respond fast while Iranian user traffic to international destinations is throttled or blocked at gateway",
      "Domestic banking layer instability — Saman Bank degraded (3375ms) but Shaparak persistently timeout; Snapp redirect loop persists; payment layer remains fragile",
      "Irancell web portal latency normalized from evening spike (was 10.6s at 16:05 UTC, now 1.36s) — evening throttling peak has fully resolved",
      "Shecan DNS stable (227ms) — evening measurement captures post-peak baseline without peak-pressure distortion",
      "IODA, OONI, RIPEstat, Tor Metrics all operational — external observatories reachable",
      "External reachability at 4.0% (43/1068 ranges) matches whitelisted gov/edu/cloud ranges — confirms tiered access model where only smaller orgs (Raya Sepehr Vira 75%, Research Org 25%, Respina 21%, Asiatech 10.6%) show external reachability while major ISPs (MCI 0%, TIC 0%, Irancell 0%, Rightel 0%) show zero external reachability"
